(As you do not say for what system you wish to compile, I'm going to
assume from your user agent that it is Windows.)

The first link is to the install instructions in the NetHack source
directory; under Windows this would be sys/winnt/Install.nt . This
document is the basic guide for compiling NetHack.

To get a C compiler for Windows, you can try Microsoft's compiler
(http://msdn.microsoft.com/visualc/vctoolkit2003) or various third party
software, such as GCC (Cygwin; http://www.cygwin.com), LCC
(http://www.cs.virginia.edu/~lcc-win32/) or Borland C
(http://www.borland.com/bcppbuilder/freecompiler/). I am using the MS
compiler or GCC, and these compilers are those for which you are most
likely to get answers here in rgrn.

The second link, then, is to the installation instructions of the
compiler of your choice. 

If everything is set up, you can proceed step-by-step from NetHack's
instructions; feel free to ask here any further questions. 

